# BroilerSmart Manual QA Test Plan

## 1. Objective

Evaluate whether the batch creation feature handles valid, invalid, and unusual inputs appropriately.

## 2. Scope

The initial test cycle covers batch names, supplier names, bird quantities, saving records, and persistence.

## 3. Test Method

Tests are performed manually. Actual behaviour is compared with expected behaviour, based on established requirements or reasonable, documented assumptions.

## 4. Test Environment

- Application: BroilerSmart
- Application version: To be recorded
- Device and operating system: To be recorded
- Test date: To be recorded

## 5. Entry Criteria

The application can be opened and the batch creation feature is accessible.

## 6. Exit Criteria

Planned tests have recorded outcomes, potential defects have sufficient reproduction details, and unresolved questions are documented.

## 7. Limitations

The application requirements may not specify every input boundary. Findings that depend on unclear requirements will be recorded as observations pending clarification.
